# PHASE 6 — TECHNICAL SEO IMPLEMENTATION

Inspect the existing technical SEO setup before making changes.

Implement appropriate improvements where necessary.

## 6.1 Page-level SEO

For every indexable page, review:

- Unique, descriptive title tag
- Relevant meta description
- One clear primary H1
- Logical heading hierarchy
- Useful and relevant page content
- Canonical URL
- Robots directives
- Open Graph metadata
- Appropriate structured data
- Internal links
- Image alt text where meaningful
- Mobile usability
- Loading performance
- Correct HTTP status and routing behavior

Do not generate identical titles and descriptions across large numbers of pages.

Do not add indexable pages with little or no useful content simply to target additional keywords.

## 6.2 Structured data

Use structured data only when the page and visible content genuinely qualify.

Evaluate appropriate types, including WebSite, Organization, BreadcrumbList, Article, and relevant SoftwareApplication or other supported types where applicable.

Use JobPosting structured data only for legitimate, current job listings that meet the applicable requirements.

Do not add fake reviews, ratings, salaries, job listings, FAQ content, or other unsupported structured data.

Validate generated JSON-LD and ensure that its claims match the actual page.

## 6.3 Architecture and internal linking

Create a logical topical architecture connecting:

- Resume/CV tools and templates
- Cover letter tools and templates
- Recommendation and reference letters
- Job application emails
- ATS and job application tracking
- Job-search resources
- Career guides
- Supporting articles and relevant country pages

Use contextual internal links and clear navigation.

Avoid orphan pages, excessive navigation links, unnecessary route aliases, and large collections of near-duplicate URLs.

If a URL changes, implement a suitable redirect where supported and preserve existing external links where possible.

Do not remove useful existing routes without a documented migration plan.

## 6.4 Sitemap, indexing and crawlability

Verify:

- XML sitemap generation
- Inclusion of intended canonical indexable URLs
- Exclusion of irrelevant, duplicate, and non-indexable URLs
- robots.txt behavior
- Canonical consistency
- Correct HTTP status codes
- Correct internal links
- SPA route refresh and direct navigation behavior
- Existing deployment and hosting constraints

Do not claim that a page is indexed by Google merely because it returns HTTP 200 locally.

Do not claim that rankings, impressions, or organic traffic have improved without actual measurement data.

## 6.5 Performance and accessibility

Preserve the current design system and responsive experience.

Inspect page performance, rendering, image handling, accessibility, semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, form labels, contrast, and major layout shifts.

Fix verified issues that can be safely addressed without breaking the application.

Do not sacrifice functionality or content quality merely to chase an arbitrary performance score.

