# PHASE 8 — NEW TOOLS, PAGES AND FEATURES MUST BE FUNCTIONAL

When a keyword justifies a new tool or feature:

1. Inspect existing components and utilities for reusable functionality.
2. Design the smallest complete implementation that satisfies the intended use case.
3. Add the correct route and navigation entry where appropriate.
4. Implement working input fields, validation, generation or processing logic, editing, and copy/export functionality where relevant.
5. Integrate the feature with existing templates and builders when useful.
6. Add appropriate loading, success, empty, and error states.
7. Make the tool responsive and accessible.
8. Add unique, useful explanatory content and relevant SEO metadata.
9. Add internal links and sitemap integration where appropriate.
10. Test the full user workflow, not just whether the page renders.

Do not build a cosmetic interface with fake output.

Do not add API-dependent AI functionality that cannot work without the required backend or credentials. If a feature requires an external API, explain the dependency and implement a working alternative only when technically appropriate.

Do not expose secret keys or credentials in client-side code.

Preserve all existing user data and avoid unnecessary changes to shared components.

